Z||000003||84Bill||06-07-2001||07:41 AM||||You must sterilize the area properly, 1000 degrees should do it. then you need to remove the contaminated soot ash and debris, I think the asbestos removing companies can handel this task. After that you must seal the area with a good watertight sealer we don't want anything seeping in. then a good coat of paint will cover it all over. GOOD LUCK!<P><BR>OMG I thaught you said TR7! oh sheeit man a CRX? OHHH man sorry dewd, your SOL bigtime! better get the wrecking ball out and I'm sorry to say your Fiero may disown you for such foul treatment. Just don't go near it for a few days and call a Fiero counselor to come have a talk with it. I can do it for nominal fee and I accept most major credit cards. I'll have to warn you. Your car may have to come with me for some longterm therapy     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> There are no guarantees that it will recover from such a tremendously traumatic event like that. What were you thinking!<P><p>[This message has been edited by 84Bill (edited 06-07-2001).]||||reg||11
